course: dictionary
lesson: 13309
title: A grievance is a complaint
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A grievance is a reason to feel upset because something seems unfair, and to want to complain about it. It can be real, or it can be only how someone feels. «Sam had a grievance against his brother, who always took the last biscuit.» Sam feels wronged, so his grievance is about something he thinks is unfair.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The workers raised a grievance with their boss about unpaid overtime.» Workers are people with jobs, and they raised it with their boss, so here a grievance is an official complaint about unfair treatment. Try swapping in complaint: does the sentence still make sense? It does.
explain: People often say they have a grievance, air a grievance, or have a sense of grievance. «Her list of grievances was long: no pocket money, early bedtimes and no pets.» A list of grievances means many complaints, each one about something that feels unfair to her.
fact: A grievance is a reason to feel upset and to complain about something unfair.
fact: A grievance can be real or imagined: it still counts if the person truly feels wronged.
fact: At work, a grievance is an official complaint a worker makes about unfair treatment.
fact: Useful phrases: have a grievance against, air a grievance, a sense of grievance, a list of grievances.
fact: Grievance is a noun. One is a grievance, and more than one is grievances.
exercise: «The workers raised a grievance with their boss.» What is a grievance here? | A kind thank-you note | *A complaint about unfair treatment | A birthday present | A short holiday
exercise: Sam says he has a grievance against his brother. What does that mean? | He has forgotten his brother's name | *He feels his brother has treated him unfairly | He is best friends with his brother | He wants to swap places with his brother
exercise: «Her list of grievances was long.» Find and copy the word that names the complaints. | list | *grievances | was | long
test: «The villagers had a real grievance: the mill owner kept all the water for himself.» Why did the villagers have a grievance? | They were bored with the village | *Because the owner treated them unfairly | They wanted a new mill | They had lost their hats
test: Which phrase means a long set of complaints? | have a grievance against | air a joke | a sense of humour | *a list of grievances
exam: Can a grievance be only imagined? | Yes, but only at school | *Yes, it can be only how someone feels | No, it must always be a proven fact | No, it is always a happy feeling
